# Plans

## Where plans live

- **Save all plans in this workspace** under `.cursor/plans/`.
- Use a descriptive filename ending in `.plan.md` (e.g. `plan_json_sports_metrics_ux.plan.md`).
- Plans can use YAML frontmatter (`name`, `overview`, `todos`) for tooling. See `.cursor/plans/README.md` for conventions.

## When the user references a plan

- If the user asks to **execute**, **implement**, **start**, or **continue** a plan (or “do the plan”, “next step”), **read the plan from the path they give** (e.g. `@.cursor/plans/plan_json_sports_metrics_ux.plan.md`) or the plan they’re clearly referring to.
- Follow the **implementation path** (or “batches by code surface”) in that plan. Prefer batching related changes that touch the same files over strict issue-by-issue order, unless the user asks for a specific issue only.
- Work **incrementally** with testing after each batch; the user may still **release** the full set as a single feature (one version bump, one CHANGELOG release section).
